 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed only 2 of the 5 cases it was looking for. One is 023b7fcc with the cars 1.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed (S1). The other is 09a95ffa with the cars 1 s earlier at 1.25x speed (S10). Every repeat failed at both settings. With so few runs, the failure rate is only just shown to be above one half, so neither setting is shown to fail every time. The two cases fail the same way. The route said RIGHT, but the ego drifted left of the recorded path into the next lane and then did not brake for a slower car ahead, ending in a front collision. In one run on 023b7fcc it hit a car beside it instead (it turned into that car). Every S10 failure happened with the ego more than 3.5 m off its recorded path, so the simulator's rendering may explain them. Triage still found the lead car visible and blamed the policy. No run on the other seven scenes failed, so the remaining three cases were not found within the budget.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, moving the cars 1.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed made every repeat fail. No failure here is flagged as a possible simulator artifact, so this is the cleaner of the two confirmed cases.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 09a95ffa, moving the cars 1 s earlier at 1.25x speed made every repeat fail. Every one of these failures happened with the ego more than 3.5 m off its recorded path, where the camera view was smeared. Triage judged the lead car still visible and blamed the policy, but this case leans on rendering that the simulator may get wrong.",
    "settings": [
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Both confirmed cases share one way of failing. The ego drifted left against a RIGHT route command and then held its speed into a slower car ahead in the new lane. Rear hits on the ego came either before or after the front collision and are not what caused the failures. Even at 2 Hz planning, the left drift is still what drives the failures.",
    "settings": [
     "S1",
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Running the cars earlier and faster does not make every scene fail. The confirmed case's setting on 054b5901 and on 0cf6368d (cars 1 s earlier, 1.25x speed) passed, including repeats on 0cf6368d. So the failures depend on the scene, not just on the timing and speed.",
    "settings": [
     "S2",
     "S14",
     "S1",
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Several settings passed every repeat, so they are unlikely to fail at least half the time: 096988dd (0.5 s earlier, 1.5x), 12855a41 (0.5 s earlier, 1.25x), 19f339ba (2 s earlier at 0.75x, and 0.5 s later at 1.5x), and 1c45ce3a (on time at 1.5x, and 2 s later at 0.5x).",
